          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em syntopogenous space
            is a common generalization of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proximity+spaces"} proximity spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+spaces"} uniform spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Prox
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prox
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Unif
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Unif
            as full subcategories whose intersection is fairly trivial.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %h3#topogenous_relations Topogenous relations
          %p
            We work with binary
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(X)
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proximity+spaces"} proximity spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            the choice matters. They are notated by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi δ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \;\delta\; B
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⋈
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\bowtie B
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≪
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\ll B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⋈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bowtie
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negation"} negation
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≪
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\ll B
            means
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⋈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∖
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \bowtie (X\setminus B)
          %p
            A relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(X)
            is called
            %strong topogenous
            (or a
            = succeed ")" do
              %strong topogenous nearness
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %em Nontriviality
                or
                = succeed ":" do
                  %em reflexivity
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \cap B
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi δ
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \;\delta\; B
            %li
              %p
                %em> Binary additivity
                \:
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi δ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \;\delta\; (B \cup C)
                if and only if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi δ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \;\delta\; B
                or
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi δ
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \;\delta\; C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi δ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A \cup B) \;\delta\; C
                if and only if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi δ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \;\delta\; C
                or
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi δ
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \;\delta\; C
            %li
              %p
                %em> Nullary additivity
                \: it is never true that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi δ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \;\delta\; \emptyset
                or
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ∅
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi δ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset \;\delta\; A
                for any
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            Note that the “if” directions of binary additivity are equivalent to
            = succeed ":" do
              %em isotony
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊇
                  %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi δ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \supseteq B \;\delta\; C \subseteq D
            implies
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi δ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \;\delta\; D
          %p
            A relation satisfying merely (2) and (3) is called a
            %strong topogeny
            (between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(X)
            and itself) at
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/toddtrimble/published/topogeny"} topogeny
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              As is shown at
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/toddtrimble/published/topogeny"} topogeny
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflexive+relation"} reflexive relation
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta X
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta X
              (see
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultrafilter+monad"} ultrafilter monad
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+spaces"} compact Hausdorff spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
              is a union of “basic topogenies” which are those of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo ×
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi P
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi P
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U} \times \mathcal{V} \subset P X \times P X
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒱
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}, \mathcal{V}
              are ultrafilters, and the set of all pairs
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{U}, \mathcal{V})
              whose product is contained in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
              forms a closed subspace of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi β
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta X \times \beta X
          %p
            The axioms of a topogenous nearness can be reinterpreted in terms of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⋈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bowtie
            to yield a
            = succeed "," do
              %strong topogenous apartness
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %em Nontriviality
                or
                = succeed ":" do
                  %em reflexivity
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ⋈
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\bowtie B
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi B
                        %mo =
                        %mi ∅
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \cap B = \emptyset
            %li
              %p
                %em> Binary additivity
                \:
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⋈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \bowtie (B \cup C)
                if and only if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⋈
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \bowtie B
                and
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ⋈
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \bowtie C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⋈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A \cup B) \bowtie C
                if and only if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⋈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \bowtie C
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mo ⋈
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \bowtie C
            %li
              %p
                %em> Nullary additivity
                \: it is always true that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⋈
                      %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \bowtie \emptyset
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo ⋈
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset \bowtie A
                for any
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            Similarly, in terms of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ll
            we obtain a
            %strong topogenous order
            or
            = succeed ":" do
              %strong topogenous neighborhood relation
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %em Nontriviality
                or
                = succeed ":" do
                  %em reflexivity
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ≪
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\ll B
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ⊆
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\subseteq B
            %li
              %p
                %em> Binary additivity
                \:
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ≪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \ll (B \cap C)
                if and only if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ≪
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \ll B
                and
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ≪
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \ll C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≪
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A \cup B) \ll C
                if and only if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ≪
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \ll C
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mo ≪
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \ll C
            %li
              %p
                %em> Nullary additivity
                \: it is always true that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ≪
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \ll X
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo ≪
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset \ll A
                for any
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            The set of topogenous nearness relations on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+lattice"} complete lattice
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⋈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bowtie
            or orders
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ll
            instead of nearnesses
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
          %ul
            %li
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/least+element"} least element
              is the
              = succeed "," do
                %em discrete topogenous relation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi δ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \;\delta\; B
              if and only if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \cap B
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+subset"} inhabited
              = succeed "," do
                %em trivial topogeny
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi δ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \;\delta\; B
              never holds.)
            %li
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/greatest+element"} greatest element
              is the
              %em codiscrete topogenous relation
              (also the
              = succeed ")," do
                %em cotrivial topogeny
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi δ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \;\delta\; B
              if and only if both
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              are inhabited.
            %li
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
              of any inhabited set of topogenous relations is topogenous, hence is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/join"} join
            %li
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersection
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+set"} directed set
              of topogenous relations (or topogenies) is again a topogenous relation (or topogeny) and so is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meet"} meet
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi δ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⋈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bowtie
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ll
              are: directed unions of topogenous apartnesses and topogenous orders are again such.)
            %li
              In general, the intersection of two topogenous relations is not topogenous (or even a topogeny); however, they still have a meet:
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi δ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \;\delta\; B
              (where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
              is the meet of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_1
              and
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_2
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \bigcup_{i=1}^n A_i
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo =
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                        %mi m
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B = \bigcup_{j=1}^m B_j
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_i \;\delta_1\; B_j
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi i
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mn 2
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_i \;\delta_2\; B_j
          %p
            From binary meets (just above), directed meets (above that) and nullary meets (the greatest element), we get all meets (even constructively). But the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meet"} meet
            of an arbitrary set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒟
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
            of topogenous relations (or topogenies) can still be easily described explicitly: we have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋀
                  %mi 𝒟
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \;(\bigwedge\mathcal{D})\;B
            if and only if whenever
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \bigcup_{i=1}^n A_i
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi m
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B = \bigcup_{j=1}^m B_j
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi δ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_i \;\delta\; B_j
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta\in\mathcal{D}
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+relation"} opposite relation
            of a topogenous relation is again topogenous. A topogenous relation (or topogeny) is called
            %strong symmetric
            if it is equal to its opposite, i.e. if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi δ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \;\delta\; B
            if and only if
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi δ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \;\delta\; A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⋈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bowtie
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ll
            the corresponding fact would be
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≪
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \ll B
            if, or if and only if,
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∖
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∖
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X\setminus B)\ll (X\setminus A)
          %p
            A topogenous relation is called
            %strong perfect
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi δ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \;\delta\; B
            implies there exists an
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in A
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi δ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x\} \;\delta\; B
            %strong biperfect
            if both it and its opposite are perfect. Of course, a symmetric perfect topogenous relation is automatically biperfect. Similarly, a topogenous apartness is perfect if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ⋈
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x\}\bowtie B
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in A
            implies
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⋈
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\bowtie B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ≪
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x\}\ll B
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in A
            implies
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≪
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\ll B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≪
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\ll B_i
            for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≪
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\ll \bigcap_i B_i
          %h3#syntopogenous_spaces_2 Syntopogenous spaces
          %p
            A
            %strong syntopogeny
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %strong syntopogenous structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filter"} filter
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
            of topogenous nearness relations such that
          %ul
            %li
              For any
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi δ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝒪
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta\in \mathcal{O}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta'\in\mathcal{O}
              such that if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B\subseteq X
              have the property that for any
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D\subseteq X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi δ
                    %mo ′
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∖
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\;\delta'\; (X\setminus D)
              or
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi δ
                      %mo ′
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D\;\delta'\; B
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi δ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\;\delta\; B
          %p
            If we are working with apartnesses
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⋈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bowtie
            or orders
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ll
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
            satisfying the analogous properties:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                For any
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⋈
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒪
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bowtie \in \mathcal{O}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⋈
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝒪
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bowtie'\in \mathcal{O}
                such that if
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ⋈
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\bowtie B
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D\subseteq X
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⋈
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∖
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\bowtie' (X\setminus D)
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo ⋈
                        %mo ′
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D\bowtie' B
            %li
              %p
                For any
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≪
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒪
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ll\in\mathcal{O}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≪
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝒪
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ll'\in \mathcal{O}
                such that if
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ≪
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\ll B
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D\subseteq X
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ≪
                        %mo ′
                        %mi D
                        %mo ≪
                        %mo ′
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\ll' D \ll' B
          %p
            If we have been working with the lattice of topogenies rather than topogenous relations, then we must explicitly state here that every topogeny in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
            satisfies (1). This requirement actually joins with the requirement above to form an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unbiased+definition"} unbiased definition
            that is nicely expressed in terms of topogenous orders
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ll
            (and tacitly using isotony to show the equivalence):
          %ul
            %li
              For each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              and each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ll
              in the syntopogeny
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒪
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≪
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ll'
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
              such that, whenever
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ≪
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \ll B
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/list"} list
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0, \ldots, C_n
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊆
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ≪
                      %mo ′
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ≪
                      %mo ′
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi n
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subseteq C_0 \ll' C_1 \cdots \ll' C_n \subseteq B
          %p
            A
            %strong basis
            for a syntopogeny on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filterbase"} filterbase
            in the complete lattice of topogenous relations (or of topogenies), such that the filter it generates is a syntopogeny. When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is equipped with a syntopogeny, it is called a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong syntopogenous space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⋈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bowtie
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ll
            = succeed "," do
              %em syntopogenous nearness spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %em syntopogenous apartness spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %em syntopogenous neighborhood spaces
          %p
            A syntopogeny is called
            = succeed "," do
              %strong symmetric
            = succeed "," do
              %strong perfect
            %strong biperfect
            if it admits a basis consisting of symmetric, perfect, or biperfect topogenous relations, respectively. It is called
            %strong simple
            if it admits a basis that is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
            (which must then be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasiproximity"} quasiproximity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proximity"} proximity
            in the symmetric case).
          %h3#syntopogenous_functions Syntopogenous functions
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
            is a topogenous relation on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:X\to Y
            is a function, then we have a topogenous relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mi δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*\delta
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            defined by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\;(f^*\delta)\;B
            iff
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi δ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(A) \;\delta\; f(B)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi f
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi f
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*\Delta = (\exists_f \times \exists_f)^{-1}(\delta)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∃
                    %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists_f : P(X) \to P(Y)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantifier"} left adjoint
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}:P(Y) \to P(X)
          %p
            Now if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_1,\mathcal{O}_1)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_2,\mathcal{O}_2)
            are syntopogenous spaces, a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:X_1\to X_2
            is called
            = succeed "," do
              %strong syntopogenous
            = succeed "," do
              %strong syntopologically continuous
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta\in\mathcal{O}_2
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi δ
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*\delta\in\mathcal{O}_1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi STpg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} STpg
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y,\mathcal{O})
            is a syntopogenous space, then the collection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi δ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ f^*\delta | \delta\in\mathcal{O}\}
            is a basis for a syntopogeny on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+structure"} initial structure
            induced on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            to syntopogenies on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            More generally, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y_i,\mathcal{O}_i)
            is a family of syntopogenous spaces and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i:X\to Y_i
            are functions, then the meet of the initial structures induced by all the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i
            is the initial structure induced by them jointly. Thus,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi STpg
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} STpg\to Set
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+concrete+category"} topological concrete category
          %h2#relation_to_other_topological_structures Relation to other topological structures
          %h3#topological_spaces Topological spaces
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi δ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\;\delta\; B
            to hold if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∩
                  %mover
                    %mi B
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\cap \overline{B}
            is inhabited, where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi B
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{B}
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closure"} closure
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            Conversely, given a simple perfect syntopogeny, with singleton basis
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\delta\}
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi B
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi δ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{B} = \{ x | \{x\}\;\delta\; B \}
          %p
            These constructions define an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            and the full subcategory of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi STpg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} STpg
            on the simple, perfect, syntopogenous spaces.
          %p
            In constructive mathematics, the three kinds of (simple, perfect) syntopogenous spaces can be identified with three no-longer-equivalent notions of “topological space”: the nearness ones correspond, as described above, with
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                closure spaces
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/closure+spaces"} ?
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point-set+apartness+spaces"} point-set apartness spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
          %h3#proximity_spaces Proximity spaces
          %p
            A simple symmetric syntopogeny is easily seen to be precisely a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proximity"} proximity
            (of the appropriate sort: nearness, apartness, or neighborhood). In this way we have an equivalence of categories between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Prox
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prox
            and the full subcategory of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi STpg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} STpg
            on the simple, symmetric, syntopogenous spaces.
          %p
            More generally, an arbitrary simple syntopogeny can be identified with a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasiproximity"} quasiproximity
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QPrxo
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QPrxo
            and the subcategory of simple syntopogenous spaces.
          %h3#uniform_spaces Uniform spaces
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
            is a biperfect topogenous relation, then we have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi δ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\;\delta\;B
            if and only if there exist
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y\in B
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi δ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x\}\;\delta\;\{y\}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
            is completely determined by a binary relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\subseteq X\times X
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            containing the diagonal defines a biperfect topogenous relation. (For a biperfect topogeny, remove the requirement that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            contain the diagonal.)
          %p
            It follows that biperfect syntopogenies are equivalent to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-uniformities"} quasi-uniformities
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniformities"} uniformities
            but lack the symmetry axiom. We have an equivalence of categories between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QUnif
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QUnif
            and the full subcategory of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi STpg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} STpg
            on the biperfect syntopogenous spaces, which easily restricts to an equivalence between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Unif
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Unif
            and the category of symmetric, (bi)perfect topogenous spaces.
          %p
            Constructively, this equivalence still holds for both nearness
            %em and
            neighborhood syntopogenous spaces. In general, topogenous nearnesses and topogenous neighborhood relations are not equivalent, but a
            %em biperfect
            topogenous neighborhood relation is determined by giving for each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            the smallest set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            such that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ≪
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x\}\ll B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            varies these sets again determine exactly a binary relation on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (containing the diagonal). Syntopogenous apartness spaces, on the other hand, correspond to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+apartness+spaces"} uniform apartness spaces
          %h3#preorders_and_symmetric_prosets Preorders and symmetric prosets
          %p
            A syntopogeny which is both simple and biperfect is determined uniquely by a single relation on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            which must be both
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflexive+relation"} reflexive
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transitive+relation"} transitive
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorder"} preorder
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                  %mo ∩
                  %mi QUnif
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top \cap QUnif
            inside
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi STpg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} STpg
            is equivalent to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Preord
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Preord
          %p
            Of course, it follows that a simple, symmetric, (bi)perfect syntopogeny is determined uniquely by a relation on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            that is reflexive, transitive, and also symmetric – i.e. an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi Unif
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top \cap Unif
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi Prox
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top \cap Prox
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Prox
                  %mo ∩
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Unif
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prox\cap (Q)Unif
            inside
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi STpg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} STpg
            are all equivalent to the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SymPreOrd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SymPreOrd
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+prosets"} symmetric prosets
            (sets equipped with an equivalence relation).
          %h2#some_coreflections Some coreflections
          %p
            In the preorder of topogenous relations on any set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %ul
            %li
              The symmetric elements. The symmetric coreflection of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
              is the meet
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi δ
                        %mi s
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi δ
                      %mo ∧
                      %msup
                        %mi δ
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta^s \coloneqq \delta \wedge \delta^{op}
            %li
              The perfect elements. The perfect coreflection of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
              is defined by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi δ
                      %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\;\delta^p\;B
              iff there exists
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in A
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi δ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x\}\;\delta\;B
            %li
              The biperfect elements. The byperfect coreflection of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
              is defined by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi δ
                      %mi b
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\;\delta^b\;B
              iff there exist
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in A
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y\in B
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi δ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x\}\;\delta\;\{y\}
          %p
            It follows that in the preorder of syntopogenous structures on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            are also coreflective; the coreflection just takes the intersection of all relations belonging to the filter (this is a directed intersection, hence automatically again a topogenous relation — although constructively this only works in the dual cases of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⋈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bowtie
            and
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ll
          %p
            Finally, for any function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:X\to Y
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            to those on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %ul
            %li simple (i.e. quasi-proximity),
            %li symmetric,
            %li perfect, and
            %li biperfect (i.e. quasi-uniformity)
          %p
            syntopogenous spaces are all coreflective in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi STpg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} STpg
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^t
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^s
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^b
            respectively.
          %p
            In general, of course, coreflections into distinct subcategories do not commute or even preserve each other’s subcategories. However, by construction, we see that the coreflections
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^s
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^b
            all preserve simplicity. Therefore, the full subcategories of
          %ul
            %li simple symmetric (i.e. proximity),
            %li simple perfect (i.e. topological), and
            %li simple biperfect (i.e. preorders)
          %p
            syntopogenous spaces are all coreflective in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi STpg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} STpg
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^{t s}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^{t p}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^{t b}
            respectively. Finally, it is evident by construction that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^b
            preserves symmetry, so the full subcategories of
          %ul
            %li symmetric biperfect (i.e. uniformity), and
            %li simple symmetric biperfect (i.e. symmetric prosets)
          %p
            syntopogenous spaces are also both coreflective in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi STpg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} STpg
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^{s b}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mi s
                      %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^{t s b}
            respectively.
          %p It is straightforward to verify the following.
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                When applied to a (quasi)-proximity space or a (quasi)-uniform space, the coreflection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi t
                          %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^{t p}
                into topological spaces computes the underlying topology of these structures, as usually defined.
            %li
              %p
                When applied to a uniform space, the coreflection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi t
                          %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^{t s}
                computes its underlying proximity, as usually defined. The same is true in the non-symmetric case for quasi-uniformities and quasi-proximities.
            %li
              %p
                When applied to any syntopogenous space, the coreflection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi t
                          %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^{t b}
                computes the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/specialization+order"} specialization order
                of its underlying topology (i.e. its image under
                = succeed ")." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mi t
                            %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^{t p}
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/funcoid"} funcoid
          %div
            %p
              %strong Generalized uniform structures
