          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              Ákos Császár,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Foundations of General Topology
          %p
            Császár uses topogenous orders
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ll
            %em basis
            for one. As usual, this is convenient for concreteness (especially in the simple case), but has the disadvantage that distinct structures can nevertheless be isomorphic via an identity function, i.e. the forgetful functor to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            is not
